Subject: [PATCH 04/14] =?UTF-8?q?scl:=20drc=5Fsize=20command=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20enforce=20max=5Fout=5Fcap=20and=20a=20slew=20limit=20by=20up?=
 =?UTF-8?q?sizing?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Neither upsize/dnsize nor buffer ever ENFORCE the library's electrical
rules: a D1 gate can silently drive 20x its max_out_cap (the only trace
is stime's printout), and on unrepaired netlists the resulting slews
leave the NLDM characterization range, where both OpenSTA and
Scl_LibLookup linearly extrapolate -- measured as a large delay inflation
against first-principles arithmetic. drc_size sweeps
the mapped network (placement-aware loads when read_place is active)
and upsizes each violator to the smallest same-function variant whose
max_out_cap covers its real load; -S adds a slew limit as further
upsizing pressure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
